Saturday evening I call my family in Mexico.
We speak by video on my laptop.
It is only early afternoon there, so nothing has happened yet today.
My parents are sitting in the living room, but today the connection is bad.
My mother's picture keeps freezing.
"Maya, can you hear us?" she asks.
"Yes, but I can't see you properly," I answer.
I explain to her what she should do.
"Please close the other apps, Mama."
"And go a bit closer to the router."
"Should I call again?" she asks.
"Yes, try that please," I say.
Mostly that is all it takes.
The screen turns black and the connection is disconnected.
A minute later the laptop rings again.
I accept the call.
Now the picture is completely sharp.
"... so we just stayed at home today!" my mother says mid-sentence.
She looks delighted and keeps talking right away.
We talk to each other for over an hour.
